
```
[Script Runner APK]  ──SSH (port 8022)──>  [Termux: sshd + nmap]
   input box  ──command──>                  installs/updates pkgs, runs nmap
   output box <──stream──                   live output (mirror view)
```

Since both apps live on the same phone, the APK just connects to `127.0.0.1:8022`. Anything you type ("scan ports", "update packages", "run ls") gets translated to shell commands and streamed back live.

## Part 1 — Termux side (one-time setup)

```bash
pkg update && pkg upgrade -y
pkg install openssh nmap -y
passwd            # set a password for SSH
sshd              # start the SSH server (port 8022)
```

Leave Termux running in the background. Optionally use `termux-wake-lock` so Android doesn't kill it.

## Part 2 — The APK (Android Studio)

**1. `app/build.gradle`** — add the SSH library:

```gradle
dependencies {
    implementation 'com.jcraft:jsch:0.1.55'
    implementation 'androidx.appcompat:appcompat:1.6.1'
    implementation 'com.google.android.material:material:1.11.0'
}
```

